From: DBY-W09 kernel-port draft
Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] arm64: dts: qcom: DBY-W09 UFS Host dual GenPD topology

The SM8250 UFS Host's existing required-opps entries point to RPMHPD
performance levels, while the inherited Host node is attached only to GCC
UFS_PHY_GDSC. For DBY-W09, declare both consumers explicitly and keep the
ordering required by the companion ROUND33 UFS driver change:

  index 0: RPMHPD MMCX
  index 1: GCC UFS_PHY_GDSC

The UFS PHY itself remains attached to GCC UFS_PHY_GDSC. This does not add
an MMCX-to-MX parent relationship or claim HOS4.3 ARC corner equivalence.

This patch targets the repository's review-only board DTS draft, not a
production kernel DTS path. It is not applied to the protected
ack18-dby-w09-dts-draft branch and has not been compiled or schema-validated.

---
 dts/dby-w09-ack18-board.dts.draft | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dts/dby-w09-ack18-board.dts.draft b/dts/dby-w09-ack18-board.dts.draft
--- a/dts/dby-w09-ack18-board.dts.draft
+++ b/dts/dby-w09-ack18-board.dts.draft
@@ -19,6 +19,8 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include <dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-sm8250.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/power/qcom,rpmhpd.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
 
 #include "sm8250.dtsi"
@@ -211,7 +213,11 @@
  *     verified HOS VCC operating window is 2.504–2.950 V.
  */
 &ufs_mem_hc {
+	power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>,
+			<&gcc UFS_PHY_GDSC>;
 	vcc-supply = <&vreg_l17a_3p0>;
 	vcc-voltage-level = <2504000 2950000>;
 	vcc-max-microamp = <800000>;
-- 
